; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Sound Waves
; CATEGORY: Science & Simulation
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     sound, waves, pitch, loudness, tone, physics
; SUMMARY:  Draws four sound waves (low, high, loud and soft) and plays each one so you can see and hear the difference.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Sound is air wiggling back and forth. The program draws four waves
;   one under the other and plays each as it is drawn:
;     a low note    - the wiggles are far apart
;     a high note   - the wiggles are close together
;     a loud note   - the wiggles are tall
;     a soft note   - the wiggles are short
;   (The computer can only make loud and soft with the volume knob,
;   so those two sound the same here. Real sound waves differ.)
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Turn your sound on and press Run. Listen while each wave is drawn.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * frequency (how many wiggles per second) is the pitch you hear
;   * amplitude (how tall the wiggles are) is how loud it sounds
;   * SIN makes the smooth up-and-down shape of a wave
;   * TONE frequency milliseconds plays a note
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add a fifth wave for a very low note of 110 hertz.
;   * Draw a wave whose wiggles get closer and closer (a siren).
;   * Play two notes at once: add two SIN values together and draw it.
; ============================================================

; Draw one wave across the screen at height :middle.
; :wiggles is how many full ups and downs fit across the screen,
; :height is how tall each one is.
to draw.wave :middle :wiggles :height :color
  setpc 15 setpensize 1
  penup setxy -300 :middle pendown setx 380
  setpc :color setpensize 3
  penup setxy -300 :middle pendown
  ; Walk across 680 steps. At each x, SIN tells us how high to go.
  ; One full wiggle is 360 degrees, so the angle grows by
  ; 360 x wiggles over the whole width.
  for [x 0 680 2] [
    setxy :x - 300 :middle + :height * sin (:x * 360 * :wiggles / 680)
  ]
  penup
end

to name.wave :middle :words
  setpc 0 setlabelheight 16
  penup setxy -390 :middle - 6 label :words
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground 7

name.wave 200 [low note]
draw.wave 200 4 40 1
tone 220 800

name.wave 70 [high note]
draw.wave 70 16 40 4
tone 880 800

name.wave -70 [loud note]
draw.wave -70 8 60 13
tone 440 800

name.wave -200 [soft note]
draw.wave -200 8 15 2
tone 440 800

print [Low notes have few wiggles, high notes have many.]
print [Loud sounds have tall wiggles, soft sounds have short ones.]
